# Vendor license issuance material.
#
# These are never tracked and never shipped. The signing key JSON carries the
# raw Ed25519 private seed, so anyone holding it can mint unlimited licenses
# against any server_id -- and the server verifies offline, so a leaked key
# cannot be revoked. The issuance log is a cross-customer business record.
#
# The patterns are unanchored on purpose: license_vendor/README.md tells the
# operator to run the commands with these exact filenames from whatever
# directory they happen to be in, so a root-anchored rule would miss the file
# one `cd` away. The earlier /license_vendor_issuance_log.jsonl rule matched
# only the repo root and left vendor_signing_key.json uncovered entirely.
vendor_signing_key.json
*signing_key*.json
vendor_public_key.pem
license.json
eval_license.json
paid_license.json
license_vendor_issuance_log.jsonl
issuance_log.jsonl
# The customer's request is not secret the way the signing key is, but it carries
# their server_id, host fingerprint and hostname, and license_vendor/README.md has
# the operator running issue-eval against it from whatever directory they are in.
license_request.json

